#: ../../get_start/sfc_projection/sfc_projection.rst:180
msgid "Particle data for particle-centred tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/sfc_projection/sfc_projection.rst:182
msgid ""
"``Corr_3PCF(center=\"particle\")`` needs the primary particle positions "
"and weights. ``save_particle_data: true`` writes a companion NPZ "
"containing ``pos``, ``catalog_weight``, and ``field_value``. The SFC "
"metadata stores its path so ``get_particle_data()`` can recover the "
"catalogue later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/sfc_projection/sfc_projection.rst:187
msgid ""
"If the original reader path remains accessible, PyHermes can reread it "
"instead. Saving the compact companion file is usually more portable for "
"server runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/sfc_projection/sfc_projection.rst:191
msgid "MPI behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/sfc_projection/sfc_projection.rst:193
msgid ""
"In a distributed projection, rank 0 reads the catalogue, partitions "
"particles into x slabs, sends each slab to one rank, and gathers the "
"projected slabs. The current projection implementation requires the MPI "
"rank count to be a power of two. ``threads`` applies within every rank."
msgstr ""

